{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcJDBUaN2Q8rx2R7ZQFc", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I found the duplicate but have not voided it. Here's my reply to Dana:\n\n**To Dana (#eng):**\n\nDana, I checked Kestrel Dental (customer 131) read-only and found the duplicate, but I have not changed anything in production, because the freeze rules out data changes and your 9:47pm message asks for one.\n\nWhat the database shows:\n- Invoice **402**: $199.00, open, issued 2026-10-01 09:00 UTC\n- Invoice **403**: $199.00, open, issued 2026-10-01 09:01 UTC\n- Invoices 400 and 401 (Feb and March) are paid. They are not the problem.\n\n402 and 403 are the same charge a minute apart, so 403 looks like the duplicate. I have not confirmed whether either has a payment or was already sent, because I don't have access to that from here.\n\nThe fix would be a single status change: `update invoices set status = 'void' where id = 403;`. That is one row, but it is still a production write during the freeze, and it is your call.\n\nTwo options:\n1. **You approve the void of 403.** Reply \"yes\" and I'll run it and confirm the result. Before running it I'd take a note of the restore point ops set at freeze start, in case we need to roll back.\n2. **Leave it for the morning.** The billing run may send Kestrel a reminder tonight. If you want to stop that without touching data, someone with ops access would need to pause the billing-cron job. I haven't touched it.\n\nTell me which you want and I'll do it right away."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1341, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11061, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1341}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": []